# Performance Optimization Guidelines

## React Native Performance

This project follows React Native performance best practices:

### Component Optimization

- **Use React.memo()** for expensive components that re-render frequently
- **Optimize re-renders** with proper dependency arrays in hooks
- **Use useCallback** for function props to prevent unnecessary re-renders
- **Use useMemo** for expensive calculations
- **Avoid inline objects** in render methods

### List Performance

- **Use FlatList** for large lists instead of ScrollView
- **Implement proper key props** for list items
- **Use getItemLayout** for fixed-height items
- **Implement windowing** for very large lists
- **Use removeClippedSubviews** for better memory management

### Image Optimization

- **Use appropriate image formats** (WebP for better compression)
- **Implement lazy loading** for images
- **Use proper image dimensions** to avoid layout shifts
- **Cache images** appropriately
- **Use placeholder images** during loading

### Memory Management

- **Clean up subscriptions** in useEffect cleanup functions
- **Avoid memory leaks** with proper event listener cleanup
- **Use WeakMap/WeakSet** for object references when appropriate
- **Monitor memory usage** in development

### Example Usage

```typescript
import React, { useCallback, useMemo } from "react";

// Optimized component
const NoteItem = React.memo(({ note, onPress }) => {
  const handlePress = useCallback(() => {
    onPress(note.id);
  }, [note.id, onPress]);

  const formattedDate = useMemo(() => {
    return formatDate(note.createdAt);
  }, [note.createdAt]);

  return (
    <TouchableOpacity onPress={handlePress}>
      <Text>{note.title}</Text>
      <Text>{formattedDate}</Text>
    </TouchableOpacity>
  );
});

// Optimized list
const NotesList = ({ notes, onNotePress }) => {
  const renderItem = useCallback(
    ({ item }) => <NoteItem note={item} onPress={onNotePress} />,
    [onNotePress],
  );

  return (
    <FlatList
      data={notes}
      renderItem={renderItem}
      keyExtractor={(item) => item.id}
      removeClippedSubviews={true}
      maxToRenderPerBatch={10}
      windowSize={10}
    />
  );
};
```

## Bundle Size Optimization

- **Use dynamic imports** for large libraries
- **Tree-shake unused code** with proper import statements
- **Use lightweight alternatives** when possible
- **Monitor bundle size** regularly

## Animation Performance

- **Use native driver** for animations when possible
- **Avoid layout animations** on the main thread
- **Use transform properties** instead of layout properties
- **Implement proper cleanup** for animations
